WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:29.780
The

00:29.780 --> 00:36.260
land that nourishes and provides sanctuary for all life, jite, refers to standing on

00:36.260 --> 00:38.220
this very land.

00:38.220 --> 00:44.540
The progress line of jite pumsae that represents the initiate that stands firmly on land to

00:44.540 --> 00:49.740
train taekwondo is the Korean vowel O.

00:49.740 --> 00:53.100
We will now take a look at the key moves of jite pumsae.

01:19.740 --> 01:26.740
Let's take a look at the key moves of jite pumsae that represent the initiate that stands

01:26.740 --> 01:29.740
firmly on land to train taekwondo.

01:49.740 --> 02:17.940
Let's take a look at the key moves of jite pumsae.

02:17.940 --> 02:31.700
Jite pumsae consists of three moves, namely sonnal olgul maki, geumgang jireugi, and mejumok

02:31.700 --> 02:43.580
yeop pyojok jigi, anpalmok bakkat maki.

02:43.580 --> 02:48.700
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of jite pumsae.

02:48.700 --> 02:54.300
Sonnal olgul maki is, as the name suggests, a technique to block the face upwards with

02:54.300 --> 02:55.900
both arms.

02:55.900 --> 03:00.880
Cross the arms so the blocking arm is outside to block the face.

03:00.880 --> 03:04.660
The hand of the blocking arm rises first.

03:04.660 --> 03:10.700
Raise the hand first at face elevation and snap the elbow upward to block.

03:10.820 --> 03:19.820
Pull the opposite fist to the back and cross the hand blade with the center line.

03:19.820 --> 03:26.820
The space between the blocking arm and forehead should be about one fist.

03:26.820 --> 03:33.740
Tilt the arm so that the fist faces upward and the elbow faces downward.

03:33.740 --> 03:38.860
Be careful not to let the elbow of the blocking arm open backwards as this will weaken the

03:39.020 --> 03:41.260
arm.

03:41.260 --> 03:46.940
The elbow must not raise first to block.

03:46.940 --> 03:51.940
Be careful not to let the blocking arm rise above the head.

03:51.940 --> 04:02.940
Geumgang jireugi is a technique to block and attack simultaneously with olgul maki and jireugi.

04:03.660 --> 04:09.820
Mejumok yeop pyojok jigi is a technique to strike the target at the side of the body

04:09.820 --> 04:15.180
at philtrum elevation with the hammer fist while spinning the torso.

04:15.180 --> 04:20.780
The elbow of the part striking the target must face downward.

04:20.780 --> 04:25.780
The hammer fist must not spin and strike the target like anmakgi.

04:25.780 --> 04:32.780
Anpalmok bakkadmakgi is a technique used to perform bakkadmakgi with the anpalmok.

04:33.100 --> 04:39.780
Cross both arms in front of the chest and block inside out.

04:39.780 --> 04:44.980
These are the four key moves of jite pumsae.

04:44.980 --> 04:51.380
We will now look at the moves in succession connecting each move.

04:51.380 --> 04:58.380
The key moves of jite first part consist of wen anpalmok bakkadmakgi, orun olgul makgi,

05:03.340 --> 05:10.340
and wen jireugi, orun anpalmok bakkadmakgi, orun olgul makgi, and orun jireugi, orun arhaemakgi,

05:24.540 --> 05:31.540
orun sonnal olgul makgi, orun abchagi, and orun sonnal goduro arhaemakgi.

05:33.940 --> 05:40.940
Slowly block the face by raising the fist diagonally from the right back.

05:41.300 --> 05:45.860
Then slowly perform wen jireugi.

05:45.860 --> 05:50.620
The arm that blocked the face should move as if you are pulling an opponent.

05:50.620 --> 05:56.260
Achieve balance in the speed and force of the pulling arm and the thrusting arm.

05:56.260 --> 06:01.100
Lower the elbow of the arm that blocked the face and slowly cross the middle with the

06:01.100 --> 06:06.140
fist that performed the thrust, exerting force in the lower abdomen.

06:06.140 --> 06:10.140
All moves and breathing must coincide during this process.

06:10.140 --> 06:15.320
When performing orun anpalmok bakkadmakgi in the previous move, push off the ground

06:15.320 --> 06:21.660
with the right foot from the orun abgubi posture and move your center to the left foot.

06:21.660 --> 06:27.500
Create a central axis on the left, turn right using the left ball as an axis, then perform

06:27.500 --> 06:31.220
wen duikubi anpalmok bakkadmakgi.

06:31.220 --> 06:36.940
When performing wen sonnal olgul makgi, move your center back and assume the sonnal olgul

06:36.940 --> 06:39.580
makgi posture.

06:39.580 --> 06:45.780
Bend the foot that performed abchagi and connect to sonnal goduro makgi.

06:45.780 --> 06:51.980
Cautions for jite first part, taking a closer look.

06:51.980 --> 06:57.140
When connecting olgul makgi and jitegi, the thrusting arm should not move excessively

06:57.140 --> 06:59.100
forward.

06:59.100 --> 07:07.100
Be careful not to let the stride become too long when setting your foot with abgubi.

07:07.100 --> 07:13.420
During orun anpalmok bakkadmakgi, do not move your center forward and back, then perform

07:13.420 --> 07:19.620
a 180-degree doradiki.

07:19.620 --> 07:27.540
The direction of the elbows should not move forward.

07:27.540 --> 07:33.740
When connecting abchagi and sonnal goduro makgi, the foot performing abchagi must not

07:33.740 --> 07:37.860
raise above the head.

07:37.860 --> 07:43.300
We will now practice the moves of jite first part in succession while watching the video.

08:07.860 --> 08:27.100
The key moves of jite second part consist of orun bakkadmakgi, wen abchagi, and wen

08:27.100 --> 08:37.780
sonnal goduro aremakgi, wen olgul makgi.

08:37.780 --> 08:48.780
Orun geumgang apjirugi, wen anmakgi, and orun goduro anmakgi, wen sonnal aremakgi,

08:48.780 --> 08:55.940
and orun abchagi, and double jirugi.

08:55.940 --> 09:00.980
Perform bakkadmakgi slowly, exerting force on the lower abdomen.

09:00.980 --> 09:06.340
Then block by crossing your left wrist and right wrist in front of your chest.

09:06.340 --> 09:10.620
The lower body must stand firm when performing the move.

09:10.620 --> 09:17.780
When performing geumgang apjirugi, raise the left arm that blocked the face to chest elevation.

09:17.780 --> 09:24.860
Then quickly block the face upward again and connect with apjirugi at the same time.

09:24.860 --> 09:30.220
Perform momtong anmakgi with the left arm that performed olgul makgi.

09:30.220 --> 09:32.420
Pull the other fist back.

09:32.460 --> 09:38.060
Then successfully pull the left arm and perform orun goduro anmakgi.

09:38.060 --> 09:43.020
The left fist should be placed next to the right elbow.

09:43.020 --> 09:49.060
Connect the two moves quickly and pay attention to your breathing.

09:49.060 --> 09:54.200
Pull and set your right foot back and perform wen sonnal aremakgi.

09:54.200 --> 09:59.180
When pulling and setting the foot, make sure to move the central axis along with the right

09:59.180 --> 10:00.980
foot.

10:00.980 --> 10:05.780
After performing orun abchagi, bend and withdraw the knee.

10:05.780 --> 10:12.980
Then complete orun jirugi when the heel of the right foot touches the ground.

10:12.980 --> 10:18.660
Then quickly connect to wen jirugi.

10:18.660 --> 10:25.420
Cautions for jittei second part, taking a closer look.

10:25.420 --> 10:31.880
When performing pakkadmakgi, execute slowly and do not exert force.

10:31.880 --> 10:37.260
When performing geumgang apjirugi, the arm blocking the face should not move excessively

10:37.260 --> 10:41.500
below the chest.

10:41.500 --> 10:48.300
It is important to connect anmakgi and goduro anmakgi naturally.

10:48.300 --> 10:55.300
After performing orun abchagi, do not connect to orun wen double jirugi.

10:55.700 --> 11:00.820
After the entire right foot touches the ground.

11:00.820 --> 11:07.180
The double jirugi must follow after the right heel touches the ground.

11:07.180 --> 11:14.180
We will now practice the moves of jittei second part in succession while watching the video.

11:25.300 --> 11:32.300
The key moves of jittei third part consist of hwangsomakgi, wen palmokare yeopmakgi,

11:32.300 --> 11:37.300
orun sonnal yeopmakgi, wen mejumok pyojokchigi, hakdari are yeopmakgi, jageun doljokgui,

11:37.300 --> 11:40.300
and wen mejumok pyojokchigi.

11:40.300 --> 11:49.300
The key moves of jittei third part consist of hwangsomakgi, wen palmokare yeopmakgi,

11:49.300 --> 12:00.300
orun sonnal yeopmakgi, wen mejumok pyojokchigi, hakdari are yeopmakgi, jageun doljokgui,

12:01.300 --> 12:05.300
orun yeopchagi, and wen are yeopmakgi,

12:07.300 --> 12:12.300
jageun doljokgui, wen yeopchagi, and orun jirugi,

12:13.300 --> 12:16.300
and orun jirugi.

12:18.300 --> 12:25.300
When performing wen palmokare yeopmakgi, your eyes should point in the direction of the blocking arm.

12:25.300 --> 12:34.300
When performing wen mejumok pyojokchigi, create a target by raising the right arm that performed sonnal yeopmakgi to philtrum elevation.

12:35.300 --> 12:40.300
Then twist your torso to the right and perform mejumok pyojokchigi with a shout.

12:43.300 --> 12:47.300
Bend your arm so that the target and your elbow turn facing each other.

12:48.300 --> 12:52.300
Then perform mejumok pyojokchigi on the palm of your right hand.

12:52.300 --> 13:03.300
When performing hakdari are yeopmakgi, pull your right foot to your left knee and perform are yeopmakgi at the same time.

13:04.300 --> 13:12.300
Assume the jageun doljokgui posture by pulling only the fist to the left waist without change in elevation.

13:13.300 --> 13:17.300
When performing orun yeopchagi and wen are yeopmakgi,

13:18.300 --> 13:25.300
quickly pull the left foot to the right knee the moment the right foot performs jichigi on the ground.

13:27.300 --> 13:31.300
Quickly change the direction of the eyes, then block.

13:33.300 --> 13:37.300
Cautions for jite third part, taking a closer look.

13:39.300 --> 13:45.300
When performing wen palmokare yeopmakgi, your eyes should not be directed forward.

13:47.300 --> 13:51.300
Your eyes should not be directed forward during sonar yeopmakgi either.

13:53.300 --> 13:59.300
Wen mejumok pyojokchigi should not be performed like anmakgi with the hammer fist spinning.

14:01.300 --> 14:06.300
When assuming the jageun doljokgui posture, the left knee must not straighten.

14:07.300 --> 14:11.300
When performing orun yeopchagi and wen are yeopmakgi,

14:12.300 --> 14:17.300
do not switch feet while jumping or pull the left foot with the right foot set.

14:21.300 --> 14:27.300
We will now practice the moves of jite third part in succession while watching the video.

14:36.300 --> 14:53.300
The key moves of jite fourth part consist of

14:53.300 --> 15:06.300
Wen sonar godoro aremakgi, orun sonar godoro makgi, orun sonar godoro aremakgi, and wen sonar godoro makgi.

15:08.300 --> 15:18.300
When connecting sonar godoro aremakgi and sonar godoro makgi, set your foot from dvikubi to dvikubi or perform doradikki.

15:19.300 --> 15:23.300
The central axis and the foot must spin simultaneously.

15:26.300 --> 15:29.300
The same elevation must be maintained at a constant level.

15:33.300 --> 15:37.300
Cautions for jite fourth part, taking a closer look.

15:40.300 --> 15:45.300
When connecting two moves, do not spin your central axis after moving your foot.

15:45.300 --> 15:50.300
The trajectory of the foot should not draw an arc when performing doradikki.

15:53.300 --> 15:59.300
We will now practice the moves of jite fourth part in succession while watching the video.

16:11.300 --> 16:14.300
This concludes the training for jite pumse.

16:15.300 --> 16:19.300
We will take another look at all the moves and master pumse.

16:45.300 --> 16:47.300
Thank you for watching.

17:15.300 --> 17:17.300
Thank you for watching.

17:46.300 --> 17:55.300
We have looked at the key moves of jite pumse and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for.

17:56.300 --> 18:00.300
Man set his foot on land, the sanctuary of life.

18:01.300 --> 18:10.300
Continue with your training, always keeping in mind the meaning of jite, the spirit of the will to live, and the land which is our sanctuary.

18:11.300 --> 18:14.300
We will see you again in the chunguan pumse video.

18:15.300 --> 18:17.300
Thanks for watching.

